      "display_title": "Issue #219: Clean up leftovers from upload content sniffing (#80)",
      "main_description_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Assignee:</strong> Pebi Sandi Pratama — Developer</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5824211765\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/216\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/216/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/216\">#216</a> (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889174949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\">#80</a>) moved upload validation to <code class=\"notranslate\">shared.DetectImageUpload</code>. It shipped with a gofmt failure, helpers that nothing calls any more, and SVG branches that can never run. Clean them up in one PR. Nothing changes for clients except one new response header.</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>gofmt:</strong> <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/shared/upload_validation_test.go</code> is not gofmt-clean (struct field and map alignment). Run <code class=\"notranslate\">gofmt -w</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Dead code</strong> (no non-test caller left):\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">helpers.AvatarExt</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">src/helpers/avatar.go</code>) and its new test <code class=\"notranslate\">src/helpers/avatar_test.go</code>. Deleting it also drops the <code class=\"notranslate\">helpers</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">action/v1/shared</code> import it introduced.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">shared.CanonicalExtFromMime</code>: only <code class=\"notranslate\">AvatarExt</code> calls it.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">shared.AllowedImageUpload</code>: only tests call it. Point those tests at <code class=\"notranslate\">DetectImageUpload</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">normalizeContentType</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/auth/update_profile.go</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">allowedExts</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">AllowedMime</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/shared/shared.go</code>.</li>\n<li>Inside <code class=\"notranslate\">DetectImageUpload</code>, the <code class=\"notranslate\">allowedMimes[detected]</code> check and the <code class=\"notranslate\">mimeToCanonicalExt[detected] == \"\"</code> check do the same job. Keep one map.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Unreachable SVG branches:</strong> the <code class=\"notranslate\">Content-Disposition: attachment</code> blocks added for SVG in <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/files/get.go</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/files/shared.go</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">sendProjectFile</code>) and <code class=\"notranslate\">src/controllers/v1/auth/avatar.go</code>. The content type there comes from <code class=\"notranslate\">MimeTypeFromExt</code>, which has no <code class=\"notranslate\">.svg</code> entry and returns <code class=\"notranslate\">application/octet-stream</code>, so <code class=\"notranslate\">mimeType == \"image/svg+xml\"</code> is never true. SVG cannot be uploaded either. Remove the blocks.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"notranslate\">X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>:</strong> no response sets it today. Set it once for every response (one Fiber middleware in <code class=\"notranslate\">cmd/api/main.go</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Why</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Two validators existing side by side (<code class=\"notranslate\">AllowedImageUpload</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">DetectImageUpload</code>) makes the next reader guess which one guards uploads. <code class=\"notranslate\">nosniff</code> closes the gap <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889174949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\">#80</a> leaves: a file with a real PNG header followed by HTML passes content sniffing. It is served as <code class=\"notranslate\">image/png</code>, so browsers do not run it, and <code class=\"notranslate\">nosniff</code> makes sure none tries to re-detect the type.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Acceptance Criteria</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">gofmt -l ./src</code> prints nothing</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> The symbols listed above are gone; <code class=\"notranslate\">go build ./...</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">go vet ./...</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">go test ./...</code> pass</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Upload behaviour unchanged: genuine PNG/JPEG/WebP still accepted, spoofed content still 400 (<code class=\"notranslate\">src/routes/v1/upload_hardening_test.go</code> stays green)</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Responses carry <code class=\"notranslate\">X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code> (one route test asserts it)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Dependencies</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Follow-up to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889174949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\">#80</a> (PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5824211765\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/216\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/216/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/216\">#216</a>, released to <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">bba62ba</code>). Start after <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889175084\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81\">#81</a> (PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5824449516\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/217\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/217/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/217\">#217</a>) merges: both touch the upload files.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">RESULT (2026-10-14)</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Shipped by PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5840054888\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/221\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/221/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/221\">#221</a> (merged to <code class=\"notranslate\">development</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">9522cbb</code>) and release PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5843048735\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/224\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/224/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/pull/224\">#224</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">e10ba20</code>).</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The dead helpers and maps listed above are gone; <code class=\"notranslate\">DetectImageUpload</code> checks <code class=\"notranslate\">mimeToCanonicalExt</code> only.</li>\n<li>The unreachable SVG <code class=\"notranslate\">Content-Disposition</code> blocks are gone from <code class=\"notranslate\">files/get.go</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">files/shared.go</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">controllers/v1/auth/avatar.go</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">upload_validation_test.go</code> is gofmt-clean. Six unrelated files (billing, members, change_password, floorplan test) still fail <code class=\"notranslate\">gofmt -l ./src</code>; they already did on <code class=\"notranslate\">development</code> before this task, so the first AC was worded too wide.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code> is set on every response in <code class=\"notranslate\">buildApp()</code>; <code class=\"notranslate\">cmd/api/main_test.go</code> fails if the middleware is removed.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">go build ./...</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">go vet ./...</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">go test ./...</code> green on the merged tree.</li>\n<li>Production check on 192.168.1.226: <code class=\"notranslate\">GET /v1/auth/me</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">GET /v1/projects</code> (no session, 401) carry <code class=\"notranslate\">X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>. The <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889174949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/80\">#80</a> and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4889175084\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/GoThruMedia/Gothru-3d-Floormap-API-GO/issues/81\">#81</a> checks still pass: spoofed uploads get 400 <code class=\"notranslate\">Unsupported file type</code>, and the file list carries no <code class=\"notranslate\">storagePath</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
